unications and working in close collaboration with the offices of the chancellor, provost, and other senior vice chancellors. 498638 Part-Time IT Help Center Support Technician Denver, CO August 31, 2026 September 07, 2026 As a part-time Help Center Support Specialist, you’ll be the friendly and knowledgeable face of the IT Help Center. You’ll work in person with students, faculty, and staff, assisting with technical support needs ranging from password resets to device troubleshooting and preparing loaner equipment. 499019 HVAC Technician Denver, CO August 31, 2026 September 18, 2026 With minimal or no supervision, this position repairs, maintains and installs heating, air conditioning and refrigeration equipment, including but not limited to boilers, pumps, fans, compressors, cooling towers, chillers, air compressors, pneumatic and electrical controls and heat exchangers. 499020 Administrative Coordinator, NWSS CoE Denver, CO August 31, 2026 September 14, 2026 The Administrative Coordinator provides administrative and operational support to the Program Manager and helps ensure continuity of Colorado NWSS CoE operations. The position supports day-to-day administrative, financial, human resources, website, and program activities and provides backup administrative coverage for the Program Manager during absences. 499014 Associate Director, Daniels Student Success Center Advising Operations and Academic Planning Denver, CO August 28, 2026 September 11, 2026 The Associate Director, Daniels Student Success Center Advising Operations and Academic Planning leads the operational infrastructure that supports student progression, academic planning, course management, and degree completion across undergraduate and graduate populations. 499015 Senior Academic Advisor, Daniels Student Success Center Advising and Engagement Denver, CO August 28, 2026 September 11, 2026 The Senior Academic Advisor in Advising and Engagement within the Daniels Student Success Center (SSC) provides proactive, relationship-centered advising to support student progression, academic planning, and connection to the Daniels student experience. 499016 Adjunct Faculty, Global and Public Affairs Denver, CO August 28, 2026 Open until filled The Josef Korbel School of Global and Public Affairs at the University of Denver is looking to hire adjunct instructors for the 2026-2027 academic year to teach a variety of undergraduate and graduate courses. 498998 LEP Tutor Denver, CO August 26, 2026 October 26, 2026 The Learning Effectiveness Program (LEP) at the University of Denver is now hiring LEP Tutors for the upcoming 2026-2027 academic year. We need tutors who have a strong background in college-level Business, Engineering/Computer Science, Humanities, Languages, Mathematics, Science, and Social Sciences from entry-level to advanced level. 499005 Japanese Instructor Denver, CO August 26, 2026 September 05, 2026 The Japanese instructor will teach elementary students Japanese with some planning time and duty, Monday – Friday between 8:15 am – 12:00 pm on full-day student contact days during the 2026-2027 school year. 499006 Student Affairs Coordinator Denver, CO August 26, 2026 September 09, 2026 Reporting to the Assistant Dean of Student Affairs, the Student Services Coordinator provides operational and front desk support for the Office of Student Affairs, as well as front desk support for the Office of Admissions and Student Financial Management. 499007 Policy Research Communications and Executive Coordinator Denver, CO August 26, 2026 September 18, 2026 Hybrid position leads the Lab's day-to-day communications while providing executive coordination to Lab leadership. This role translates research and policy analysis into materials leadership and external audiences can act on quickly—drafting, editing, and designing content—and manages leadership's calendars, supports briefing preparation, and ensures follow-through on external commitments. The position also serves as backup coverage for core operations functions and requires reliable transportation for occasional, sometimes last-minute, delivery of materials, supplies, and catering within the Denver metro area. 499012 Adjunct Faculty/Overload Academic Year 2026-2027, Daniels College of Business Denver, CO August 26, 2026 Open until filled The Daniels College of Business at the University of Denver is looking to hire adjunct instructors for the 2026-2027 academic year to teach a variety of courses.  This posting will be utilized to seek applicants for both teaching and non-teaching functions for adjunct and faculty overload. 498976 Seasonal Graduate Admissions Assistant Denver, CO August 24, 2026 September 18, 2026 This is a temporary, in-person, non-benefitted position in the Office of Graduate Education. 498999 Painter III Denver, CO August 24, 2026 September 07, 2026 This position performs skilled work in preparing surfaces for painting and wallpapering, applying paint and finishes to equipment, furniture, buildings, and other structures, and installing and repairing ceramic tile. 499002 Department of Geography and the Environment Adjunct/Overload AY 2026-2027 Denver, CO August 24, 2026 Open until filled This is a general posting that will serve to create a pool of applicants for adjunct faculty openings throughout the 2026-2027 academic year. Should we have an opening and be interested in pursuing your application, we will contact you with specific information. 498973 Clinical Line, 10-month, Half- or Full-Time, Assistant Rank Faculty Position, PsyD Program Denver, CO August 13, 2026 September 13, 2026 The PsyD program at the Graduate School of Professional Psychology (GSPP) at the University of Denver (DU) seeks to hire multiple faculty for 10-month, benefited, clinical-track positions to begin as soon as possible, with a preference for November 1, 2026. 498981 Ritchie Center Event Operations Associate Denver, CO August 11, 2026 September 30, 2026 Event Operation Associates ar