      "description": "Jobs@DU | University of Denver Skip to Content Current Students Alumni Families Neighbors Faculty Staff Businesses Event Portal Newman Center Ritchie Center Kennedy Mountain Campus DU Bookstore Cable Center Museum of Anthropology Vicki Myhren Gallery Evans Chapel Weddings University of Denver HRIC UTL Explore Jobs@DU New Employees HRIC Directory Labor Law Postings Employee Handbook HRIC Services Policies Resources For Back Cart The cart is empty. Total $0.00 Checkout Interested in more? Search Courses Close Search Human Resources & Inclusive Community Employment Services I-9 Process for Employees I-9 Process for Supervisors Employment Verification Name Change Process Meet the Employment Services Team Talent Acquisition & Development Talent Acquisition & Jobs@DU Onboarding & New Hire Orientation Performance Management Learning & Development DU Learn (Canvas Catalog) Engagement & Recognition Mentor Program Meet the TA&D Team Benefits Current Benefits Plans Enroll or Change Benefits Mandatory Annual Notices Vacation & Leave Programs Paid Holidays Forms Retirement Plan: TIAA Retiree Benefits Tuition Waiver Tuition Exchange Program Meet the Benefits Team Well-being Foundational Well-being Mental Well-being Spiritual and Relational Well-being Physical Well-being Well-being Events Pregnancy, Lactation Rooms and Family Resources Compensation Job Families Salary Grades Compliance & Policies for Compensation Compensation Resources Meet the Compensation Team HR Partners Employee Handbook Separations Meet the HR Partner Team About HRIC HRIC Strategic Plan What's New in HRIC? Story Mosaic HRIC Bridge Takeovers & Town Halls HRIC UTL Explore Jobs@DU New Employees HRIC Directory Labor Law Postings Employee Handbook HRIC Services Policies Resources For Search Search Input Submit Search Toggle Menu Jobs@DU Talent Acquisition & Development Explore this Section Talent Acquisition & Jobs@DU Hiring Managers & Business Officers Equal Pay for Equal Work Act Internal Notice of Filing of Labor Condition Application Non-Benefited Staff Request Form Together We Can Do More The University is always looking for creative problem solvers, critical thinkers, and lifelong learners who want to know more and do more. At DU, we champion difference-makers. Our community uses their natural talents and learned skills to improve the public good and to tackle today's critical issues. Click links below for page sections: Join the Team Life at DU DU Faculty & Staff Benefits Additional Resources Join the Team Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Student Employment Life at DU Make an Impact Be part of a dynamic team united by a bold vision: to create a great private University dedicated to the public good. Community Denver is one of the nation’s best cities for new careers. No matter your interests, you’ll be in the perfect place to embark on a fulfilling professional life. Advance Your Career As part of the DU community you will have endless opportunities to learn, grow, and thrive. The University of Denver Culture Across the University of Denver’s many divisions, departments, and offices, supervisors are searching for new employees who strive to excel and innovate, prize integrity, and who value the opportunity to engage with the community. At the University of Denver, our culture is steeped in ethics and social responsibility. As a result, our faculty and students represent a wide array of perspectives and enjoy the healthy dialogue that grows out of diversity. For all their differences, the members of our community are united by a common purpose: They're determined to confront society's most pressing challenges—everything from world health and the global economy to access to education. Statement on Inclusive Excellence As the University of Denver prepares to meet the exciting challenges of the growing, thriving and remarkably diverse city in which we live as well as the needs of a changing nation, we will continue to be guided by the principles of Inclusive Excellence. – Chancellor Jeremy Haefner DU Staff & Faculty Benefits DU offers a wide range of benefit choices including three medical plan options, a tuition waiver program and a wellness program. For more detailed information visit our Benefits website. Time Off DU offers many leave programs, as well as: 15 days of vacation a year 12 sick days a year Seven holidays along with five days during winter break Tuition Waiver The tuition waiver is designed to enable benefited employees and retirees, their spouses and partners, and/or their dependent children under the age of 25 to enroll in for-credit courses at the University of Denver with reduced or no tuition charges. Retirement Plan After a year of service, DU will match your 4 percent contributions to the University retirement plan with an 8 percent match, for a combined contribution equal to 12 percent of your appointed salary. Employee Perks RTD EcoPass DU Employee Discounts - Travel, entertainment, ski pass and more! Discounted tickets for DU cultural and sporting events Explore All Benefits Click here for our Benefits website! Additional Resources Human Resources & Inclusive Community HRIC Website ADA Accommodations In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of Denver policy, DU provides reasonable accommodations: When an applicant with a disability needs an accommodation in order to be considered for a job or cannot utilize the online application system; when an employee with a disability needs an accommodation to enable them to perform the essential functions of the job or to gain access to the workplace; and when an employee with a disability needs an accommodation to enjoy equal benefits and privileges of employment. Visit DU Accessibility to learn more about reasonable accommodations and accessibility. To request reasonable accommodations please contact the ADA Coordinator in The Office of Equal Opportunity & Title IX (EOIX) at ADA.Coordinator@du.edu or by calling 303-871-3941. Contact Talent Acquisition & Development Team 303-871-2979 303-871-2979 Mary Reed Building, 4th Floor 2199 S. University Blvd. Denver, CO 80208 Follow Us: \" \" \" \" \" See Posts Footer Menu Maps Jobs Contact Privacy Policy Feedback Consent Preferences Disclosures Copyright ©2026 University of Denver. | All rights reserved. | The University of Denver is an equal opportunity institution Start Your Application Undergraduate Applicants We accept the Common App, a universal application that can be sent to many schools. Common App First-Year Students Transfer Students Bachelor Completions All Students Graduate Applicants Go to the graduate admission application to submit your information. For information on admission requirements, visit the graduate academic programs page and locate your program of interest. Apply Now Graduate Application Explore Programs Graduate Academic Programs × Start Your Application Graduate Applicants Go to the graduate admission application to submit your information. For information on admission requirements, visit the graduate academic programs page and locate your program of interest. Apply Now Graduate Application Explore Programs Graduate Academic Programs × Take The First Step Undergraduates Contact Undergraduate Admission Request Info Graduates Request Graduate Program Information Request Info × Start Your Application: Undergraduate Applicants We accept the Common App, a universal application that can be sent to many schools. Common App First-Year Students Transfer Students Bachelor Completions All Students × See Our Campus Undergraduates View our visit options and schedule your trip to the DU campus. Schedule a Visit Graduates Find your graduate program representative and schedule a visit. Schedule a Visit × Disclosures The University of Denver admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to students at the school. It does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. If interested in more information, please explore DU’s Consumer Disclosures , the Office of Equal Opportunity & Office of Title IX and HEERF Disclosures . × Important Links for Navigating COVID Government Bodies Centers for Disease Control & Prevention Colorado Department of Health & Environment Healthcare Services Kaiser Permanente DU's Health & Counseling Center ×"
